#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-top: live view of Claude Code usage, in the spirit of nvtop.

Plan limits (5-hour, weekly, and per-model weekly such as Fable) are asked from the
`claude` command every 60 seconds. This sends no prompt and uses none of your limits,
and it covers usage everywhere (terminal, VS Code, desktop, web). The status line
script (~/.claude/usage-monitor/statusline.py) also saves them after every terminal
reply; whichever is newer is shown. Token counts come from Claude Code's local logs
in ~/.claude/projects.

The layout adapts to the window: narrow windows drop less important columns, short
windows drop whole sections (least important first), spare height makes the activity
graph taller, and windows 140+ columns wide split into two columns.

Keys: q quit, r rescan logs and re-check limits now, t next color theme (T previous).
The theme is remembered.
  claude-top --once               print one plain-text snapshot and exit
  claude-top --once --size 80x24  snapshot at a given width x height
  claude-top --theme lagoon       start with a theme (also remembered for next time)
  claude-top --themes             list themes: claude, midnight, lagoon, ember, paper, classic
  claude-top --transparent        keep the terminal's own background color
  claude-top --once --color       force colors in a snapshot (--no-color to turn off)
  claude-top --check-every 120    check plan limits every 120 seconds (minimum 30)
  claude-top --no-check           never run `claude`; use only the status line's numbers
"""
